# 116. DEFINITION OF DONE

The UI is complete when:

* A company can create an organization.
* Users can log in.
* Users see only authorized projects.
* A project can be created.
* Contract information can be maintained.
* BOQ can be imported and managed.
* Budget can be tracked.
* Schedule can be created.
* Gantt can be viewed.
* Site progress can be recorded.
* Daily reports can be submitted.
* Photos can be attached.
* Manpower can be tracked.
* Equipment can be tracked.
* Materials can be tracked.
* Material requests can be created.
* Procurement can be managed.
* Subcontractors can be managed.
* Measurements can be recorded.
* Bills can be prepared.
* Quality inspections can be performed.
* NCRs can be managed.
* Safety incidents can be recorded.
* RFIs can be managed.
* Drawings can be versioned.
* Documents can be managed.
* Meetings and action items can be tracked.
* Issues can be managed.
* Project risks can be tracked.
* Reports can be generated.
* Approvals can be managed.
* Snags can be tracked.
* Handover can be completed.
* Audit history is available.
* All major workflows are permission-aware.
* The system works on desktop, tablet and mobile.
* The architecture supports future ERP modules.

